      en: "Gagu is a peaceful village in the northeastern part of Ilfov County, belonging to the Dascălu commune, and is known for its quiet, almost secluded atmosphere. Situated away from the major highways, Gagu offers an authentic rural backdrop characterized by vast fields and small local ponds. The village's history has been tied to agriculture for centuries, with cereal farming serving as the primary livelihood for its residents. Its layout is typical of the Romanian plains, featuring houses lined up along a central axis. In recent years, Gagu has been increasingly discovered by nature enthusiasts who value the region's unspoiled character compared to the bustling suburbs of Bucharest. The village maintains an authentic charm, underscored by its traditional architecture and a slow, steady pace of life.",
