      en: "Dascălu is a commune in northern Ilfov County, known for its lush green surroundings and its steady transition from a farming community into a sought-after suburban area. The village is located in a zone that was once part of the famous Vlăsiei Forests, a heritage still evident in the scattered patches of old woodland surrounding the area. Historically focused on crop cultivation, Dascălu's proximity to Bucharest has made it a popular residential choice for professionals working in the capital. Recent years have seen significant infrastructure upgrades, including improved access to the A3 motorway. Despite the influx of modern housing, the commune's core retains its traditional feel, centered around a historic church and pre-war public buildings. Geographically, Dascălu offers a blend of open agricultural fields and forests, ensuring high air quality and a desirable living environment.",
