      en: "Cornetu is a commune in southwestern Ilfov County, conveniently located along the DN6 national road connecting Bucharest to Alexandria. It is composed of two villages, Cornetu and Buda, and lies on the left bank of the Argeș River near the Mihăilești reservoir. The area's geography is defined by its proximity to these major water bodies, making it a popular spot for fishing and outdoor leisure. Historically, Cornetu is noted for the Dormition of the Virgin Church, built in the late 18th century by the famous chronicler Stoica Ludescu, which remains a key cultural landmark. Recently, the commune has experienced significant economic growth, with various businesses and logistics centers establishing themselves along the main road. The residential sector has also expanded, attracting people from Bucharest who appreciate the natural surroundings and the short commute. Cornetu offers a balanced environment where historical heritage meets modern commercial activity at the edge of the metropolitan area.",
